# Implementation Plan — Complete Pipeline Architecture Overhaul

## Problem Diagnosis

Looking at your screenshot and codebase, I can identify **4 root causes** of the corrupted, black, and stuttering stream:

1. **Single Shared Processing Loop** — `detection_service._processing_loop()` reads a frame from `camera_manager`, runs SCRFD + ByteTrack + ArcFace + FAISS, **then** publishes a new annotated frame. The camera capture thread (`stream.py`) and the AI processing loop share the **same `latest_frame` buffer and the same `threading.Lock`**. When ArcFace inference takes 80–400ms (CPU), the lock is held while the camera thread is trying to store a new raw frame. This causes the corrupt/black frames you see.

2. **Frame Corruption via Shared Mutable Buffer** — The annotated frame in `detection_service.latest_annotated_frame` is a **reference to a mutated NumPy array**, not a safe copy. The MJPEG stream generator reads it at the same time the detection loop writes to it, producing torn/partial frames.

3. **No Rate Control on Detection** — Detection (SCRFD) runs on every frame at camera FPS (~15–30 FPS). ArcFace runs inside the same loop. This means the entire pipeline collapses when there are many faces, blocking the stream.

4. **Global Singleton `camera_manager`** — Only one camera uses the global `camera_manager`. Multiple cameras cannot run independently; they share a single stream buffer.

---

## Architecture Overview

```
[RTSP Camera]
     │
     ▼
[Capture Thread]  ──→  [LatestFrameBuffer]  ──→  [Stream Worker Thread]
                              │                          │
                              ▼                          ▼
                    [Detection Worker]            [MJPEG → Browser]
                    (SCRFD @ 8 FPS)
                              │
                              ▼
                    [ByteTrack Tracker]
                    (Every detection)
                              │
                              ▼
                    [RecognitionWorker]
                    (ArcFace @ async queue)
                              │
                              ▼
                    [Track Cache / Results]
                              │
                              ▼
                    [Overlay Renderer]
                    (Draws on raw frame copy)
                              │
                              ▼
                    [AnnotatedFrameBuffer]
```

Every camera owns its own full set of these workers. Isolation is complete.

